# Nothing but the length is named off `word` and it is read under an index, so the front end writes "a text or a list" at the binding, as it does for a parameter. One test tells one part, and the
# walk kept the list: every text failed it twice, at the length and in front of the inner loop, and ran a generic read of the length and the closed copy. The word at a binding now counts as the word
# of a parameter does: the loop whose turns hold elements against elements asks in front for a text, what is no text runs the loop as it would be walked without that guess (it asks for a list),
# and in a loop the failing side of the guess at the length asks for a text.
# f1 = mirrored
# RUN(COUNT): compile TextsOrListsAskedForWhereElementsAreHeldAgainstElements mechanisms=all
# COUNT-NOT: statistic TextsOrListsAskedForWhereElementsAreHeldAgainstElements 0
# RUN(FORM): walk f1 mechanisms=all
